# Caching rules for the console's static client build. Security headers are NOT
# set here — they are applied per-response in workers/app.ts (and the document
# CSP in entry.server.tsx, where the per-request nonce lives), which covers the
# SSR responses these files accompany.
#
# Vite content-hashes everything under /assets/, so a URL only changes when its
# bytes do. Without a rule here these inherited the Workers Assets default of
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — the edge cached them, but every browser
# still paid a revalidation round-trip for each chunk on every navigation.
#
# Cache-Control belongs ONLY in this block: every matching rule is applied and
# the values are concatenated, so a second rule covering these paths would land
# both directives on one response, and the stricter one wins.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
